{"id":"R0318","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Standalone local DNN perception per UAV; only downstream tracked object states are fused between agents.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","we propose a two-part framework for trust-based assured","Primary research contribution proposing an assured sensor fusion framework."],["E2","PDF",7,"6.2 Dataset Generation","We place 50 agents in the environment","Evaluated multi-agent aerial autonomy setting with multiple UAVs."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.2.1 Perception","perception model based on deep neural networks (DNNs)","Local DNN perception runs standalone per agent without collaborative DNN inference."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.3.2 Fusion","distributed data fusion (DDF) handles fusing tracked objects","Collaboration fuses downstream tracked object states rather than neural model inference workloads."],["E4","PDF",8,"7 Assured Distributed Data Fusion Experiments","randomly select a subset of 25 agents","Simulation-based experimental evaluation in CARLA and Monte Carlo trials."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ICCPS '25, May 6-9, 2025, Irvine, CA, USA","Event May 2025 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2025-05-07)."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","we propose a two-part framework for trust-based assured","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","https://iccps.acm.org/2025/accepted-papers/index.html",0,"Accepted Papers","Trust-Based Assured Sensor Fusion in Distributed Aerial Autonomy","Confirmed accepted main-track ICCPS 2025 paper by R. Spencer Hallyburton and Miroslav Pajic."],["E7","https://iccps.acm.org/2025/call-for-papers/index.html",0,"Call for Papers","ICCPS 2025 will employ a light-weight double-blind review","Confirms peer-reviewed ICCPS 2025 main conference track policy."]]}
{"id":"R0321","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated on six non-UAV benchmark datasets on a single GPU; no multi-UAV setting or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",5,"3 Problem Description","the MP-FTD detection framework is proposed","Primary research contribution proposing an anomaly and task detection framework."],["E2","PDF",12,"5.1 Dataset","use six publicly available real-world datasets","Evaluated on MSL, SMAP, SMD, SWaT, WADI, and UCR datasets; no UAVs evaluated."],["E3","PDF",14,"5.3 Experimental Setup","implemented using Pytorch 1.9 with a single NVIDIA","Standalone single-GPU model execution; no collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",11,"5 Experimental Results and Analysis","use six publicly available real-world datasets","Empirical evaluation across six datasets with baseline comparisons and ablations."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: October 2024","Issue date October 2024 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2024-10-04)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","the MP-FTD detection framework is proposed","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",19,"Publication History","Received 30 November 2023; revised 23 July 2024","Peer-reviewed journal article in ACM Transactions on Internet Technology with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0324","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Empirical study of centralized LLM API calls generating SysML diagrams; no evaluated multi-UAV system or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","conducted an empirical study of LLMs performance and","Primary empirical study evaluating LLM behavior-model generation."],["E2","PDF",5,"4.3 Dataset Construction (Table 2)","Drone Swarm Combat System","Drone swarm appears only as one static SysML requirement case, not an evaluated multi-UAV architecture."],["E3","PDF",6,"4.5 LLMs Selection","Closed-source models were accessed via official APIs","Standalone centralized LLM inference via APIs; no collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",7,"5 Results and Analysis of RQ1","Closed-source models were accessed via official APIs","Empirical evaluation of multiple LLMs across SysML behavior diagram generation tasks."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Internetware 2025, June 20-22, 2025, Trondheim, Norway","Event June 2025 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2025-10-27)."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Generating SysML Behavior Models via Large Language Models","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","https://conf.researchr.org/track/internetware-2025/internetware-2025-research-track",0,"Accepted Papers & Review Policy","conference will employ a double-anonymous review process","Confirmed peer-reviewed Internetware 2025 Research Track paper with exact title and authors."]]}
{"id":"R0351","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Single-UAV power-line inspection and deicing platform running standalone YOLOv5; no multi-UAV topology or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"2.1 Hardware System","The UAV inspection platform designed in this paper","Primary system design for UAV power transmission line inspection and deicing."],["E2","PDF",2,"2.1 Hardware System","hardware system of the UAV platform","Evaluated topology is a single UAV platform with a ground control center; multi-UAV only cited in related work."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.1 Experimental Analysis","adopted the improved YOLOv5 algorithm over YOLOv5","Standalone single-UAV YOLOv5 object detection without collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"3.1 Experimental Analysis","adopted the improved YOLOv5 algorithm over YOLOv5","Experimental analysis of detection, deicing efficiency, stability, and coverage."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","CSAIDE 2025, March 07-09, 2025, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia","Event March 2025 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2025-07, month only)."],["E6","PDF",2,"2.1 Hardware System","The UAV inspection platform designed in this paper","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","https://2025.csaide.net/contact",0,"Review Policy","All paper review process will be completed by","CSAIDE 2025 archive confirms Program Committee and invited-expert peer review; Publication page confirms ACM ICPS proceedings."],["E7","https://2025.csaide.net/Publication",0,"Publication","All accepted full papers will be published in","Confirms CSAIDE 2025 accepted full papers published in ACM ICPS."]]}
{"id":"R0367","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Simulated generic cloud and edge devices for distributed neural network training; no evaluated multi-UAV system or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a mechanism, called Digital Twin-Enabled Edge AI","Primary research contribution proposing a digital twin-enabled edge AI scheduling mechanism."],["E2","PDF",14,"5.1 Experimental Setup","optimizing the training accuracy of AI tasks","Simulated topology uses a cloud server and generic edge devices; multi-UAV appears only in related work."],["E3","PDF",6,"3.2.1 Task Splitting","split the task of training large-scale neural network","Focuses on distributed neural network model training rather than collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",14,"5 Experiment and the Results","optimizing the training accuracy of AI tasks","Java simulation experiments comparing proposed heuristic against baseline scheduling methods."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: September 2022","Issue date September 2022 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2022-09-15)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a mechanism, called Digital Twin-Enabled Edge AI","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",20,"Publication History","Received October 2021; revised January 2022; accepted February","Peer-reviewed journal article in ACM Transactions on Sensor Networks with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0373","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Multi-UAV nest deployment, but neural point-cloud recognition runs offline on a single remote server GPU rather than collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose Auto-UIT, an automated system for UAV power","Primary system contribution for automated UAV inspection trajectory generation."],["E2","PDF",12,"8.2 Inspection Performance","deployed across four UAV nests in the remote","Real-world deployment operates across four UAV nests in a UAV network."],["E3","PDF",9,"7.1.1 Implementation","conducting experiments on an NVIDIA Tesla A100 GPU","Neural pylon recognition executes on a single server GPU rather than collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E3","PDF",11,"8.1 System Integration","integrated into the system's remote control platform, which","Remote control platform centrally processes point cloud data for trajectory generation."],["E4","PDF",9,"7 Performance Evaluation","conducting experiments on an NVIDIA Tesla A100 GPU","Evaluated on a 3D pylon dataset and a multi-month real-world field deployment."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ACM MOBICOM '25, November 4-8, 2025, Hong Kong","Event November 2025 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2025-11-21)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose Auto-UIT, an automated system for UAV power","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","https://sigmobile.org/mobicom/2025/accepted.html",0,"Accepted Papers (Winter Round)","Auto-UIT: Automating UAV Inspection Trajectory by Recognizing Pylon","Confirmed MobiCom 2025 accepted paper (exact DOI and same nine authors with two positions swapped)."],["E7","https://www.sigmobile.org/mobicom/2025/cfp.html",0,"Call for Papers","All submissions will be evaluated through double-blind reviewing","Confirms MobiCom 2025 double-blind peer review policy."]]}
{"id":"R0384","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E2","E3"],"reason":"Assessed local PDF is an arXiv v4 preprint (2026-08-31), and evaluation uses 2D MPE reinforcement learning rather than multi-UAV collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","introduces SUB-PLAY, a novel black-box attack framework","Primary research contribution proposing a multi-agent reinforcement learning framework (neutral eligibility only)."],["E2","PDF",7,"5.1 Setup","adopt two-dimensional environments, Predator-prey and World Communication","Evaluated in 2D Multi Particle Environments; drone swarms are only motivating examples."],["E3","PDF",7,"5.1 Setup","adopt two-dimensional environments, Predator-prey and World Communication","Evaluates MARL policies rather than collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference workloads."],["E4","PDF",7,"5 Evaluation","adopt two-dimensional environments, Predator-prey and World Communication","Simulation-based experimental evaluation across multiple multi-agent scenarios."],["E5","PDF",1,"Preprint Stamp","arXiv:2402.03741v4 [cs.LG] 31 Aug 2026","Assessed arXiv v4 version date 2026-08-31 is within window; arXiv web URL inaccessible to browse."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","introduces SUB-PLAY, a novel black-box attack framework","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",1,"Preprint Stamp","arXiv:2402.03741v4 [cs.LG] 31 Aug 2026","Assessed local file is an arXiv v4 preprint dated after CCS '24, not the peer-reviewed version of record; excluded under P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0400","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Single-UAV AirSim evaluation of runtime sensor-switching middleware; no multi-UAV setting or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a capability-based sensors abstraction model","Primary research contribution proposing a capability-based runtime sensor management model."],["E2","PDF",7,"4.1 Experimental Environment","AirSim simulates the UAV with sensors","Evaluated with a single simulated UAV carrying EO and IR sensors; multi-UAV only in related work."],["E3","PDF",7,"4.1 Experimental Environment","The UAV carries EO and IR image sensors","Performs runtime sensor selection rather than distributed or collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",7,"4 Experimental Verification","AirSim simulates the UAV with sensors","AirSim simulation experiments evaluating identification and power metrics."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Internetware 2023, August 04-06, 2023, Hangzhou, China","Event August 2023 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2023-10-05)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a capability-based sensors abstraction model","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","https://conf.researchr.org/home/internetware-2023",0,"Review Policy","Internetware 2023 conference will employ a double-anonymous review","Confirms Internetware 2023 double-anonymous peer-reviewed conference proceedings."]]}
{"id":"R0409","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated on simulated FPGA sensor nodes offloading generic jobs via RL policies; no evaluated multi-UAV system or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","compares two different methods—Q-learning and shallow neural","Primary research contribution comparing Q-learning and shallow neural networks for self-aware agents."],["E2","PDF",14,"5 Evaluation","characterized from an Elastic Node v4","Evaluated on simulated reconfigurable FPGA sensor devices; drone swarms are only illustrative examples."],["E3","PDF",14,"5 Evaluation","characterized from an Elastic Node v4","Learns action policies for generic computation offloading/batching, not collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",14,"5 Evaluation","characterized from an Elastic Node v4","Simulation-based experimental evaluation using Elastic Node v4 hardware power models."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: December 2021","Issue date December 2021 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2021-12-20)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","compares two different methods—Q-learning and shallow neural","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",25,"Publication History","Received January 2021; revised August 2021; accepted September","Peer-reviewed journal article in ACM Transactions on Autonomous and Adaptive Systems with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0432","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated on point-cloud benchmarks and a single ground robot (TurtleBot3) with one Jetson; no multi-UAV setting or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","proposes VPRNet - a sequential decision-making voxel-based lightweight","Primary research contribution proposing a voxel-based point cloud registration network."],["E2","PDF",10,"5.1 Experimental Setup","TurtleBot3 Burger equipped with one heterogeneous embedded platform","Evaluated on ModelNet40, 7Scenes, and one ground robot; multi-UAV only mentioned in introduction."],["E3","PDF",10,"5.1 Experimental Setup","TurtleBot3 Burger equipped with one heterogeneous embedded platform","Standalone single-device inference on one Jetson AGX Xavier without collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",10,"5 Experiment and Evaluation","TurtleBot3 Burger equipped with one heterogeneous embedded platform","Experimental evaluation across three datasets with baselines, profiling, and ablations."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: September 2023","Issue date September 2023 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2023-09-13)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","proposes VPRNet - a sequential decision-making voxel-based lightweight","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",19,"Publication History","Received January 2023; revised May 2023; accepted June","Peer-reviewed journal article in PACMHCI with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0438","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Assessed local PDF is a HAL author preprint (hal-04511870v1), and multi-sUAS coordination exchanges mission coordinates via MQTT rather than collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"Abstract","propose a publish-subscribe architecture that enables the exchange","Primary research contribution proposing a publish-subscribe self-adaptation architecture for sUAS."],["E2","PDF",7,"5.1 Test and Validation Platform","multi-sUAS DroneResponse platform [25, 26, 2, 8]","Evaluated on a multi-sUAS platform with four hexacopters."],["E3","PDF",7,"5.2 Test Cases","propose a publish-subscribe architecture that enables the exchange","Onboard detection publishes MQTT coordinates for MAPE-K mission-state switching, not collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",7,"5 Preliminary Evaluation in the Field","multi-sUAS DroneResponse platform [25, 26, 2, 8]","Preliminary simulation and physical field evaluation across test cases."],["E5","PDF",1,"HAL Cover","Submitted on 19 Mar 2024","Assessed HAL preprint dated 2024-03-19 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2024-08-06)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a publish-subscribe architecture that enables the exchange","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",2,"Header Banner","PREPRINT - accepted for publication at the 12th","Assessed local file is a HAL author preprint (hal-04511870v1), not the published ACM proceedings version; excluded under P03 E7."],["E7","https://conf.researchr.org/home/icse-2024/sesos-2024",0,"SESoS 2024 Program & Policy","judged by at least three reviewers","Confirms SESoS 2024 workshop acceptance and peer review, but assessed local PDF remains a preprint."]]}
{"id":"R0453","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated on street-view road segmentation datasets (Cityscapes, Camvid) on a single GPU; no UAVs or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","presents a novel model, the Multi-Attention Class Feature","Primary research contribution proposing the MCFNet real-time scene parsing network."],["E2","PDF",9,"4.1 Datasets","use 1 GPU (Tesla V100) to run all","Evaluated on Cityscapes and Camvid road street-view datasets; no UAVs in method or evaluation."],["E3","PDF",10,"4.2 Implementation Details","use 1 GPU (Tesla V100) to run all","Standalone single-GPU CNN inference; no collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",9,"4 Experiments and Analysis","use 1 GPU (Tesla V100) to run all","Empirical evaluation with ablations and baseline comparisons on two segmentation benchmarks."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: March 2024","Issue date March 2024 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2024-03-08)."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","presents a novel model, the Multi-Attention Class Feature","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",18,"Publication History","Received 22 February 2023; revised 11 October 2023","Peer-reviewed journal article in ACM TOMM with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0465","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Conceptual workshop proposal lacking empirical or analytical evaluation (fails E7 completeness and E4), with no evaluated multi-UAV setting or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","introduces a framework to prevent TDoS","Primary conceptual framework contribution (neutral eligibility only)."],["E2","PDF",4,"4.2 High-level architectural vision","introduces a framework to prevent TDoS","Proposes a generic multi-edge NFV tactical architecture; UAVs appear only as passing mentions."],["E3","PDF",5,"5 Mitigation Approach","introduces a framework to prevent TDoS","Describes OODA/SON resource-scaling workflows rather than collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",8,"6 Conclusions","step of this research line is to implement","Explicitly defers implementation and empirical evaluation to future work; no experimental or mathematical performance evaluation."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ARES 2021, August 17-20, 2021, Vienna, Austria","Event August 2021 within window; Crossref URL inaccessible (Codex-supplied published-online 2021-08-17)."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","introduces a framework to prevent TDoS","Full text verified in English on original body page."],["E7","PDF",8,"6 Conclusions","step of this research line is to implement","Fails P03 E7 completeness requirement because no evaluation results are reported; CSA 2021 workshop review policy page inaccessible."],["E7","https://2021.ares-conference.eu/conference-2021/accepted-workshop-papers/index.html",0,"Accepted Workshop Papers (CSA)","Adaptive Mitigation of Tactical Denial of Sustainability","Confirmed accepted in ARES 2021 CSA workshop track, though CSA workshop-specific peer-review page could not be opened."]]}
